<ontology/use_varnish_paint_lacquer/use_varnish_paint_lacquer__0207__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. T, T" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Tar used in Varnish, Paint & Lacquer: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. T, T"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "The cobalt, or whatever colour is employed, should be ground upon a porphyry slab, with a varnish prepared as follows:--A pint of linseed oil is to be boiled to the consistence of thick honey, along with 4 ounces of rosin, half a pound of tar, and half a pint of oil of amber."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .
